"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nAfter walking around the market, we stopped by the cafe near the entrance for a quick break.  \nOrdered a Long Black as usual and settled into an outdoor table.\n\nThe wind was blowing hard and it looked like rain was coming any second, then it cleared up again out of nowhere.  \nTypical Melbourne weather — completely unpredictable.\n\n\n\nAt the restaurant next door, some older folks were leisurely enjoying drinks and a meal.  \nThat relaxed, unhurried scene looked genuinely lovely.\n\nThe coffee was reliably decent.  \nYet another reminder that Australian coffee is consistently above average wherever you go.\n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"